# THE PYTHON PACKAGES THE ATOMS BINARY'S TOOLS CONTAINER CARRIES (atoms_tools_python.go).
# Every package an atom's script imports, or an atom execs, is in this venv at
# BUILD time; nothing resolves a package when an atom runs. The chains named the
# same sets through `uv run --with` / `uvx --from` and resolved them live,
# unpinned, on every cold cache.
#
# requirements.txt is the lock: exact versions and hashes for the whole closure,
# the install is --require-hashes, and a wheel that does not match is a build
# that fails rather than a different program. Regenerate it from this directory:
#
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.14 \
#     --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 -o requirements.txt
#
# WHO NEEDS WHAT
#   pyyaml          ops:declaration, ops:metrics (infra's and flux's own tools)
#   tomli           the dies checkers' `--with tomli>=2.0` (3.14 has tomllib; kept so the set is the chains')
#   jsonschema      dies:schema, dies:findings, dies:schemas
#   ansible-core    ops:ansible (ansible-playbook --syntax-check)
#   ansible-lint    ops:ansible
#   copier          template:render-matrix (checks.CopierVersion; a test holds the two equal)
pyyaml
tomli>=2.0
jsonschema>=4.20
ansible-core
ansible-lint
copier==9.18.2
